# Mirrors the production list in grafana/grafana's .browserslistrc — a plugin has to run in
# whatever browsers Grafana itself supports.
#
# Nothing has to point rspack at this file: it looks for a browser list on its own and uses it to
# pick the syntax for the module loader and runtime code it wraps around our bundle. Dropping the
# file would cost ~29KB of unnecessary ES5 output.
#
# Our own source is compiled by swc, and that target is set in `.config/rspack/rspack.config.ts`
# (es2022 today) rather than derived from this list. The two agree in practice — every browser
# below supports es2022 — so there's nothing to override.
#
# Kept as a single list rather than grafana's [dev]/[production] split: a plugin that compiles
# differently in dev than in production hides browser-only bugs from local testing.
last 2 Firefox versions
last 2 Chrome versions
last 2 Safari versions
last 2 Edge versions
last 1 ios_saf versions
last 1 and_chr versions
last 1 samsung versions
